    "background_story": "Alfredo was a brilliant but disorganized scientist who spent most of his days in his cluttered laboratory. His workspace was a testament to his chaotic mind, with papers, notes, and reminders scattered everywhere. One day, his wife, Maria, had had enough and presented him with a simple corkboard, insisting that he use it to keep track of his thoughts and tasks. At first, Alfredo was skeptical, but soon he found himself pinning up notes, reminders, and even inspirational quotes on the board. The corkboard became the central hub of his creative process, helping him to visualize his ideas and connect the dots between seemingly unrelated concepts. As he worked on his groundbreaking project, the corkboard remained his trusted companion, a symbol of Maria's love and support. With the corkboard's help, Alfredo finally completed his life's work, a revolutionary new material that changed the world.",
